0009 - Daemon integration
=========================

How the local API, the peer API and the cert endpoints behave when the daemon runs as root outside an app sandbox.

concern   : daemon-integration
files     : 5
upstream  : squashed android patch d6a7411 (tailscale v1.98.5 -> v1.98.8), 2026-07-13
apply     : git apply patches/0009-daemon-integration.patch

Regrouped by concern from the upstream squashed patch - the ten commits named in
that squash are not recoverable from it, so this is a reviewed regrouping, not a
recovery. The split is lossless and machine-checked; see patches/MANIFEST.md.
Everything above the first "diff --git" is a preamble and is ignored by git apply.

diff --git a/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go b/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
index b5a0a353cd785..8b84d601f8001 100644
--- a/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
+++ b/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go
@@ -7103,7 +7103,14 @@ func exitNodeCanProxyDNS(nm *netmap.NetworkMap, peers map[tailcfg.NodeID]tailcfg
 	}
 	for _, p := range peers {
 		if p.StableID() == exitNodeID && peerCanProxyDNS(p) {
-			return peerAPIBase(nm, p) + "/dns-query", true
+			base := peerAPIBase(nm, p)
+			// When peerCanProxyDNS report as true but no peerAPIBase return empty
+			// Example: exit-node peerapi empty because force relogin with different auth url ( need to restart daemon )
+			if base == "" {
+				return "", false
+			}
+			dohURL = base + "/dns-query"
+			return dohURL, true
 		}
 	}
 	return "", false
